<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Yukong final '96 net falls.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Yukong final '96 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net					   68.21 vs   103.20</p>
<p>Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>	common shares			   12    vs    12</p>
<p>	preferred shares			13    vs    13</p>
<p>    Turnover				 8,322.13 vs 6,593.34</p>
<p>    Profit before tax			 93.12 vs   135.22</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  40.32 (gain) vs 29.82 (loss)</p>
<p>NOTE - Yukong Ltd is South Korea's largest oil refinery. Its share capital increased by 11.72 million shares to 74.83 million in 1996 due to conversion of equity-linked bonds, rights and bonus offerings. The company earlier said it expected the net profit for 1996 to be about 65 billion won on turnover of about 8.3 trillion won.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
